#library-shell-grid.library-notes-compact #notes-sync-fold-hint {
    height: $ds-size-1;
    min-height: $ds-size-1;
    max-height: $ds-size-1;
    text-wrap: nowrap;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

/* task-32217 (critique #9 row 14): the screen-wide density rule.
   A pane with nothing open gives its columns to its sibling. The horizontal
   half is not CSS -- it is the resolver's own empty-work-pane branch
   (Utils/adaptive_reader_state.py, the ``reader_has_item`` block Media and
   Notes already used); Prompts, Skills, Collections and Conversations now
   pass that flag, so no per-canvas width rule can drift from it. The
   vertical half (a primary content box takes the pane's remaining height,
   its actions directly beneath) is already shipped for the surfaces this
   branch owns: #library-prompt-editor-content and
   #library-media-viewer-content both carry `height: 1fr` above. The note
   editor's Body box (#library-note-body) is the one clause still bounded,
   and it belongs to the Notes branch of this wave.

   The landing is the third case: at 235 columns it painted a ten-line hub
   across ~190 cells, so its lines ran far past a readable measure. Capped
   here rather than given invented content -- what the hub should GROW is a
   product decision this wave does not own. */
#library-landing-canvas {
    max-width: $ds-size-96;
}
